{"name":"Navy Bean","hex":"#e0dccf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"navy bean","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A white bean of a variety of common bean (Phaseolus vulgaris). .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/navy_bean"}],"entries":[{"title":"Navy bean","blocks":[{"text":"The navy bean, haricot bean, Jigna bean, pearl haricot bean, Boston bean, white pea bean, or pea bean is a variety of the common bean native to the Americas, where it was first domesticated. It is a dry white bean that is smaller than many other types of white beans, and has an oval, slightly flattened shape. It features in such dishes as baked beans, various soups such as Senate bean soup, and bean pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Phaseolus_vulgaris_white_beans%2C_witte_boon.jpg/330px-Phaseolus_vulgaris_white_beans%2C_witte_boon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navy_bean","wikidata":"Q17141829"},{"title":"Navy","blocks":[{"text":"A navy, naval force, military maritime fleet, war navy, or maritime force is the branch of a state's armed forces principally designated for naval and amphibious warfare; namely, lake-borne, riverine, littoral, or ocean-borne combat operations and related functions. It includes anything conducted by surface ships, amphibious ships, submarines, and seaborne aviation, as well as ancillary support, communications, training, and other fields."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/The_Hermione_being_escorted_by_the_USS_Mitscher_%28DDG-57%29_%281%29.jpg/330px-The_Hermione_being_escorted_by_the_USS_Mitscher_%28DDG-57%29_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navy","wikidata":"Q4508"},{"title":"Bean","blocks":[{"text":"A bean is the seed of plants in many genera of the legume family (Fabaceae) used as a vegetable for human consumption or animal feed. The seeds are sold fresh or preserved through drying (a pulse). Beans have been cultivated since the seventh millennium BCE in Thailand, and since the second millennium BCE in Europe and in Peru. Most beans, with the exception of peas, are summer crops. As legumes, the plants fix nitrogen and form seeds with a high protein content. They are produced on a scale of millions of tons annually in many countries, with India as the largest producer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/French_beans_J1.JPG/330px-French_beans_J1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bean","wikidata":"Q379813"},{"title":"Navy blue","blocks":[{"text":"Navy blue, also known simply as navy, is a dark shade of the color blue. The name navy blue originally referred to the color of uniforms worn by officers in the Royal Navy. In the late 18th century, the Royal Navy adopted the color for its sailors' uniforms, partly due to the practical reason that dark colors were less prone to showing dirt and wear during long sea voyages. The color became so associated with naval service that it came to be known simply as \"navy blue.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Flickr_-_Official_U.S._Navy_Imagery_-_The_Blue_Angels_fly_in_formation..jpg/330px-Flickr_-_Official_U.S._Navy_Imagery_-_The_Blue_Angels_fly_in_formation..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navy_blue","wikidata":"Q5975887"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/US_Navy_050409-N-9693M-436_White_House_Chef_Culinary_Specialist_1st_Class_Ernesto_Alvarez_serves_Navy_Bean_soup_to_visitors_at_the_Navy_Memorial.jpg/500px-US_Navy_050409-N-9693M-436_White_House_Chef_Culinary_Specialist_1st_Class_Ernesto_Alvarez_serves_Navy_Bean_soup_to_visitors_at_the_Navy_Memorial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/US_Navy_050409-N-9693M-436_White_House_Chef_Culinary_Specialist_1st_Class_Ernesto_Alvarez_serves_Navy_Bean_soup_to_visitors_at_the_Navy_Memorial.jpg/1280px-US_Navy_050409-N-9693M-436_White_House_Chef_Culinary_Specialist_1st_Class_Ernesto_Alvarez_serves_Navy_Bean_soup_to_visitors_at_the_Navy_Memorial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/US_Navy_050409-N-9693M-436_White_House_Chef_Culinary_Specialist_1st_Class_Ernesto_Alvarez_serves_Navy_Bean_soup_to_visitors_at_the_Navy_Memorial.jpg/500px-US_Navy_050409-N-9693M-436_White_House_Chef_Culinary_Specialist_1st_Class_Ernesto_Alvarez_serves_Navy_Bean_soup_to_visitors_at_the_Navy_Memorial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Navy beans being served at the Navy Memorial (2007)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUS_Navy_050409-N-9693M-436_White_House_Chef_Culinary_Specialist_1st_Class_Ernesto_Alvarez_serves_Navy_Bean_soup_to_visitors_at_the_Navy_Memorial.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/U_995_Laboe.JPG/500px-U_995_Laboe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/U_995_Laboe.JPG/1280px-U_995_Laboe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/U_995_Laboe.JPG/500px-U_995_Laboe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The German submarine U-995, which served during World War II, pictured in 2012.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AU_995_Laboe.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb